<title>FRANCE: SIDO predicts lower French 1996 soybean crop.</title>
<headline>SIDO predicts lower French 1996 soybean crop.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>France may harvest a 1996 soybean crop of 250,000 tonnes, down from 260,000 in 1995, French oilseeds and protein seeds association SIDO said on Wednesday .</p>
<p>In its first estimate for soybeans in the new 1996/97 season, SIDO linked the decline to a 10 percent fall in sowings to 90,000 hectares from 100,000.</p>
<p>Yields were expected to increase to 2.8 tonnes from 2.6, SIDO said in its September report.</p>
<p>It pegged soybean crushings at 530,000 tonnes, up from 512,000 in the previous season.</p>
<p>Soybean exports to the rest of the European Union were forecast at 30,000 tonnes, unchanged from 1995/96.</p>
<p>This would leave France with a carryover of 92,000 tonnes at end June 1997 against 102,000 at end June 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
